      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c1475afb7ce126e9e0e3a39|full_name}: to me it sounds like they want to stop enforcing performance rules and just suggest to visitors what options to change in VRChat client.\n\nI wonder what the lag time will be for server side stats. I have a habit of uploading changes to avatar shortly before logging in, but I don't attend events so it's fine either way.\n\nThe goal is to only load avatar that will actually be shown, to avoid a hitch where a heavy avatar is loaded and then unloaded, so I kinda expect VRChat to consider un tested avatars as very poor.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-26T09:21:55.129Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please allow us to optionally disable the downloading of any avatar unless it has been tagged as have being processed for server side performance metrics.\n\nThis allows community groups and event organisers to provide a viable option for not enforcing \"no very poor avatar\" policies whilst not all avatars on the platform have not been inspected and given a server side performance metric yet.\n\nThe fallback/imposter system can be used in the place of the original avatar.",
